{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":81990,"name":"Josh Cannon","username":"thejcannon","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/thejcannon/{size}/23759_2.png","created_at":"2023-01-19T21:20:44.771Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThis already exists in \u003ca href=\"https://www.attrs.org/en/21.2.0/init.html#converters\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eattrs\u003c/a\u003e, and has great benefits for type-narrowing code (e.g. \u003ccode\u003econverter=tuple\u003c/code\u003e has an \u003ccode\u003e__init__\u003c/code\u003e accepting any iterable, but the field type is \u003ccode\u003etuple\u003c/code\u003e).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMy own specific purposes are for a case where we can’t use 3rdparty, so using \u003ccode\u003eattrs\u003c/code\u003e isn’t a solution.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, this would help shore some of the gap between type checkers and \u003ccode\u003eattrs\u003c/code\u003e, as even with \u003ccode\u003edataclass_transform\u003c/code\u003e this isn’t supported.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis also helps free users from attempting to roll their own (possibly incorrect) \u003ccode\u003e__init__\u003c/code\u003e. E.g. did you get the right type for the unary arg to \u003ccode\u003edict\u003c/code\u003e’s constructor for all your \u003ccode\u003edict\u003c/code\u003e fields?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e(I floated the idea on typing-sig to add this only to \u003ccode\u003edataclass_transform\u003c/code\u003e and they suggested just adding it to the stdlib)\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2023-01-19T21:24:06.149Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2752,"reads":108,"readers_count":107,"score":13856.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":22956,"topic_slug":"add-converter-to-dataclass-field","display_username":"Josh Cannon","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://www.attrs.org/en/21.2.0/init.html#converters","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Initialization - attrs 21.2.0 documentation","clicks":58}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":5}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":10330,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/add-converter-to-dataclass-field/22956/1","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":5}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":5,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":82071,"name":"Thomas Kehrenberg","username":"tmk","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/tmk/{size}/10935_2.png","created_at":"2023-01-20T09:45:52.875Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eIn the \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0681/#converter-field-specifier-parameter\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003erejected ideas section of the dataclass_transform PEP\u003c/a\u003e it says this regarding the \u003ccode\u003econverter\u003c/code\u003e field:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is tricky to support since the parameter type in the synthesized \u003ccode\u003e__init__\u003c/code\u003e method needs to accept uncovered values, but the resulting field is typed according to the output of the converter.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e[…]\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThere may be no good way to support this because there’s not enough information to derive the type of the input parameter. One possible solution would be to add support for a \u003ccode\u003econverter\u003c/code\u003e field specifier parameter but then use the \u003ccode\u003eAny\u003c/code\u003e type for the corresponding parameter in the \u003ccode\u003e__init__\u003c/code\u003e method.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIs this still an issue? I’m actually a bit confused by this section, because it seems to work fine in \u003ccode\u003eattrs\u003c/code\u003e?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile we’re adding features from attrs to the stdlib, I would really like to have the \u003ccode\u003ealias\u003c/code\u003e field that was introduced in attrs 22.2.0 (and which is also supported by \u003ccode\u003edataclass_transform\u003c/code\u003e!)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre data-code-wrap=\"python\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-python\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u0026gt;\u0026gt; from attrs import define, field\n\u0026gt;\u0026gt;\u0026gt; @define\n... class C:\n...    _x: int = field(alias=\"x\")\n\u0026gt;\u0026gt;\u0026gt; inspect.signature(C.__init__)\n\u0026lt;Signature (self, x: int) -\u0026gt; None\u0026gt;\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou could then emulate the converter functionality like this:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre data-code-wrap=\"python\"\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-python\"\u003efrom functools import cached_property\nfrom attrs import define, field\n\n@define(slots=False)\nclass C:\n    _x: str = field(alias=\"x\")\n\n    @cached_property\n    def x(self) -\u0026gt; int:\n        return int(self._x)  # conversion\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ebut this is of course much more verbose.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2023-01-20T09:45:52.875Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":41,"reads":93,"readers_count":92,"score":243.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":22956,"topic_slug":"add-converter-to-dataclass-field","display_username":"Thomas Kehrenberg","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0681/#converter-field-specifier-parameter","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 681 – Data Class Transforms | peps.python.org","clicks":30}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":6709,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/add-converter-to-dataclass-field/22956/2","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":82114,"name":"Josh Cannon","username":"thejcannon","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/thejcannon/{size}/23759_2.png","created_at":"2023-01-20T14:58:30.375Z","cooked":"\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIs this still an issue? …\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI don’t think so. \u003ca href=\"https://mail.python.org/archives/list/typing-sig@python.org/message/7SDEVKQHONDOL5B6DUU7TIHMIA4ASQIR/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eJelle Zijlstra also didn’t think so\u003c/a\u003e on typing-sig. And it makes sense. The converter’s output type should be the field type, and the unary input becomes the \u003ccode\u003e__init__\u003c/code\u003e param type.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMy own specific use-case here is in a library that requires truly immutable dataclasses, so we use \u003ccode\u003efrozen=True\u003c/code\u003e dataclass with immutable types (like \u003ccode\u003etuple)\u003c/code\u003e. In that regard, the cached property way of doing things is a double-whammy.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’d prefer to keep the resulting PEP single and focused to just \u003ccode\u003econverter\u003c/code\u003e \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/apple/smile.png?v=12\" title=\":smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2023-01-20T14:58:30.375Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":2,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":11,"reads":82,"readers_count":81,"score":106.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":22956,"topic_slug":"add-converter-to-dataclass-field","display_username":"Josh Cannon","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://mail.python.org/archives/list/typing-sig@python.org/message/7SDEVKQHONDOL5B6DUU7TIHMIA4ASQIR/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Mailman 3 [Typing-sig] Re: dataclass_transform support for converter field descriptor parameter - Typing-sig - python.org","clicks":25}],"read":true,"user_title":"","reply_to_user":{"id":6709,"username":"tmk","name":"Thomas Kehrenberg","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/tmk/{size}/10935_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":2}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":10330,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/add-converter-to-dataclass-field/22956/3","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":2}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":2,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":82187,"name":"Dutcho","username":"Dutcho","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/dutcho/{size}/7074_2.png","created_at":"2023-01-21T07:15:11.885Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI tried conversion in \u003ccode\u003e__post_init__\u003c/code\u003e, but\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ethe field annotation then needs to be the \u003ccode\u003eUnion\u003c/code\u003e of pre- and post-conversion types, which confuses human readers and type checkers\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003econversion in \u003ccode\u003e__post_init__\u003c/code\u003e violates any \u003ccode\u003efrozen=True\u003c/code\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis idea would solve both, so I’d be happy to see it implemented.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2023-01-23T06:52:13.566Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":3,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":19,"reads":77,"readers_count":76,"score":125.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":22956,"topic_slug":"add-converter-to-dataclass-field","display_username":"Dutcho","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","reply_to_user":{"id":10330,"username":"thejcannon","name":"Josh Cannon","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/thejcannon/{size}/23759_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":7138,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/add-converter-to-dataclass-field/22956/4","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":fa